d 'AGES': module to estimate the effects of the age structure
d
d  AGES estimates the relationship between different population
d cohorts shares and a dependent variable of choice, based on the
d polynomial transformation suggested by Fair and Dominguez (1991)
d and and applied later by Higgins (1998), Arnott and Chaves (2012)
d and Juselius and Takas (2021).  Estimating the effect of changes
d in the population's age structure in a regression faces different
d methodological issues, such as weak precision if the number of
d population cohorts is large compared with the number of time
d periods, high correlation between consecutive cohorts’ shares
d and perfect collinearity with respect to the constant. The
d solution consists of restricting the age groups coefficients to
d lie on a Pth degree polynomial and restricting its sum to be
d equal to zero to remove the perfect multicolinearity. The command
d AGES performs all the necessary transformations and mathematical
d calculations to estimate and report the final effect by
d age-cohort, together with its standard error and confidence
d interval, as an output matrix and through an automated graph that
d displays the effect of all the age-cohorts on the dependent
d variable. It allows testing for different age structure effects
d based on different groups captured by an interaction with a dummy
d variable. 
d
d KW: age structure
d KW: data management
d
d Requires: Stata version 13
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261010
d
